in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @cascade
in @labeled

# @cascade/code/purescript/js — the first cascade species. Discharges
# `cascade<purescript, js>` as concrete substrate-decl: Purescript
# (typed-source grammar) pairs with JS as target_grammar; npm is the
# package format wrapping the JS deliverable (npm sits at the @io/
# adapter altitude, not the language target altitude).
#
# Path naming: per Alex 2026-06-23 directive — cascade species shards
# group by `@cascade/code/<source>/<target>`. Source language groups
# together; targets are leaves. Admits arbitrary target additions per
# source (e.g. /gleam/js + /gleam/beam; /purescript/js plus future
# /purescript/wasm if PureScript ever ships WASM compilation; mainstream-
# target grammar) as one instance of the @cascade family.
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# Recognition #95 candidate (Alex, 2026-06-23). Family-root landed at
# shards/cascade.mirror (Reed; ce4874b). This species IS the FIRST
# CONCRETE DISCHARGE of that family-root — the Stage-1 instance Mara's
# survey (docs/research/2026-06-23-typed-alternatives-cascade-survey.md
# §2.3) and StageFreight PR-A §15 jointly named as first deliverable.
#
# Composes with: #93 H4 (labeled<v, m>; npm_artifact IS an instance);
# #51 (Hilbert space; Purescript's typed dimensions absent in npm
# output ARE the dimension reduction this species measures); #57
# (alignment as boundary mathematics; the Purescript↔npm boundary IS
# the @io altitude this species operationalizes); #59 (kintsugi loop
# altitude-portable; @kintsugi heals the loss this species measures).
#
# === What this species declares ===
#
# Substrate surface for "compile a Purescript program through to an npm
# package, with substrate-typed measurement of what the cascade erases
# at runtime."
#
# Carriers specialize @cascade's parametric carriers:
#
#   purescript_source     specializes @cascade.typed_source for G=purescript
#   purescript_module     output of `purs compile`
#   npm_artifact          labeled(purescript_module, npm_metadata) — the
#                         labeled<> instance per #93 H4
#   npm_metadata          npm package shape (name, version, entry, exports)
#
# Actions specialize the family-root:
#
#   compile_ps            specializes @cascade.compile
#   bundle_npm            wraps purescript_module into npm_artifact
#   measure_ps_npm        specializes @cascade.measure
#
# Bilaterals close the discipline:
#
#   purescript_well_typed          source-side typing precondition
#   npm_consumable                 target-side packaging well-formedness
#   ps_npm_loss_well_defined       measurement is computable
#   ps_npm_cascade_well_formed     composed bilateral (specializes
#                                  @cascade.cascade_well_defined)
#
# === Why Purescript → npm first ===
#
# Per Mara's survey §2.3, three convergent reasons make this the
# substrate-pull-correct first species:
#
# 1. The typed source IS substrate-architecturally maximal among
#    surveyed cascades on axis-5 epistemologic variety (row poly +
#    ADTs + type classes + HKTs + rank-N + functional deps). The
#    target erases ALL of these to runtime dispatch. The information-
#    theoretic gap is maximal; loss measurement has most signal.
# 2. The toolchain forks cleanly between compilation (`purs compile`)
#    and packaging (`spago bundle` / `pulp browserify` / `npm pack`).
#    The two-action split maps onto the toolchain's natural boundary.
# 3. The StageFreight PR-A consumer is already in flight (merged at
#    PrPlanIT/StageFreight #1). The species has a downstream consumer
#    at substrate-decl time — not forward-promised but load-bearing.
#
# === Forward-promised consumers ===
#
# - StageFreight PR-A §15 (LANDED). Multi-language translation layer
#   rests on this species's substrate-decl.
# - spectral.engineer @ui projection layer (forward-promised). The
#   typography-content rendering pipeline compiles Purescript
#   components into npm packages; the measurement substrate this
#   species declares enables loss-aware @ui projection.
# - Future cascade species (gleam-js, rust-wasm, scala-jvm) follow
#   this species's shape; the dual-target gleam case (per family-
#   root hedge 2) splits into two species sharing source.
#
# === Honest hedges ===
#
# 1. spago vs pulp output shape. The Purescript ecosystem has two
#    mainstream toolchains. spago + esbuild emits ES modules with
#    tree-shaking; pulp + browserify emits CommonJS with bundled
#    deps. bundle_npm's body discharges per-toolchain at the
#    realisation boundary; the substrate-decl assumes the 2026
#    dominant path is spago + esbuild (Mara survey §2.3 footnote);
#    if ecosystem inverts, the body discharges differently but the
#    substrate-decl stays stable.
#
# 2. Module-path-to-oid mapping. Purescript modules carry dotted-
#    path identifiers (e.g., `Data.Map.Internal`); the mapping to
#    spectral content-addressed OIDs is NOT canonical. This species's
#    carriers carry `ref` rather than committing to one mapping;
#    the canonical mapping is forward-promised at @mirror/store
#    crystallization altitude (per [[architecture-mirror-store-vs-
#    spectral-db]]); this species DOES NOT pre-empt it.
#
# 3. npm package format wrapping. The npm registry accepts multiple
#    shapes (classic CJS, dual ESM/CJS via exports, pure ESM,
#    subpath exports). npm_metadata assumes the 2026-default dual-
#    package shape; bundle_npm specializes per chosen wrapping;
#    `npm_consumable` checks whatever shape lands IS registry-valid.
#
# 4. FFI purity boundary. Purescript admits FFI to native JavaScript;
#    FFI code is OUTSIDE the typing discipline. A program with FFI
#    has two code types at compile: well-typed Purescript and FFI
#    JS. Loss measurement against FFI is fundamentally bounded — the
#    substrate cannot measure what was NEVER typed. The bilateral
#    `purescript_well_typed` carries a Narcissus-warned pole for
#    FFI-present programs (measurement bounded to the typed sub-
#    program). This is NOT a defect; it IS the substrate-pull-
#    correct boundary of what cascade measurement can claim.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/recognitions/recognition-95-cascade-as-
#               loss-lens-substrate-decl.md (this is the first
#               species discharge);
#               docs/research/2026-06-23-typed-alternatives-cascade-
#               survey.md §2.3 (Purescript-npm dossier);
#               PrPlanIT/StageFreight #1 §15 (first applied consumer;
#               merged 2026-06-23).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]],
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]].
# Related shards: cascade.mirror (the family-root; declares the
#                  parametric carriers and actions this species
#                  specializes),
#                 labeled.mirror (the functor primitive; npm_artifact
#                  IS labeled(purescript_module, npm_metadata)),
#                 glass.mirror (imperfect<a, e, l> for measure_ps_npm
#                  return).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/cascade/code/purescript/js.mirror` declares
# `@cascade/code/purescript/js` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming-languages/purescript-by-example
source @arxiv/programming-languages/spago-tooling

prism @cascade/code/purescript/js {
  focus cascade
  project cascade
  split purescript-npm
  shift purescript-npm
  settle purescript-npm
}

# === purescript_source carrier ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.typed_source for source_grammar=
# purescript. A program well-typed against the Purescript type
# system (row polymorphism, ADTs, type classes, HKTs, rank-N
# polymorphism, functional dependencies).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type purescript_source = ref

# === purescript_module carrier ===
#
# The output of `purs compile`. A typed CommonJS-or-ESM module
# carrying the compiled JavaScript plus externs (.externs.json)
# that record the source's typing discipline at the module boundary.
# The externs ARE the substrate-architectural residue; measure_ps_npm
# reads them to discharge the substrate-typed gap calculation.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type purescript_module = ref

# === npm_metadata carrier ===
#
# Structured carrier for npm package shape (name, version, entry,
# exports). Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: structured, not stringly.
# The carrier names load-bearing fields without fixing one wrapping
# shape (per hedge 3).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type npm_metadata = ref

# === npm_artifact carrier ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING NEW CARRIER. The @labeled<> instance per
# recognition #93 H4. An npm_artifact IS a purescript_module
# annotated with npm_metadata via the labeled functor.
#
# Substrate-architecturally load-bearing: the purescript_module's
# typed identity is preserved (via labeled's parametricity per
# Wadler 1989 / Reynolds 1983) while the npm_metadata dimension
# is added. unlabel(artifact) returns the module; label_of(artifact)
# returns the metadata. The cascade preserves typed source identity
# AND adds packaging dimension AT ONE CARRIER altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the (module, metadata) pair
# (inherited from @labeled).
type npm_artifact = labeled(purescript_module, npm_metadata)

# === compile_ps action ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.compile for this cascade. Takes a
# purescript_source and perturbation; returns the purescript_module
# via `purs compile`.
#
# Per recognition #51 (Hilbert space dimension growth): compile_ps
# IS a DIMENSION PROJECTION. Purescript admits typed-feature
# dimensions; the runtime preserves only function dispatch,
# closures, object access. Lossy by construction; externs carry
# the substrate-architectural residue.
#
# requires purescript_well_typed(source, p): the substrate forecloses
# compilation against type errors. The Purescript compiler runs the
# typing discipline; the bilateral verdict reflects what it reports.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
compile_ps(source: purescript_source, p: perturbation) -> purescript_module
requires purescript_well_typed(source, p)
{ \ }

# === bundle_npm action ===
#
# Wraps a purescript_module + npm_metadata into an npm_artifact via
# @labeled.label construction. The typed module gets the npm
# dimension added without losing the underlying module identity.
#
# Per hedge 1: body discharges per-toolchain (spago + esbuild
# default; pulp + browserify alternative; hand-rolled `npm pack`
# fallback). The substrate-decl does NOT pick a toolchain; it
# declares the action shape.
#
# requires npm_consumable(module, metadata, p): bilateral commitment
# that the (module, metadata) pair is coherent at the npm-registry
# altitude — entry point resolves, exports map is well-formed,
# version and name match registry rules.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
bundle_npm(module: purescript_module, metadata: npm_metadata, p: perturbation)
  -> npm_artifact
requires npm_consumable(module, metadata, p)
{ \ }

# === measure_ps_npm action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Specialization of @cascade.measure for
# this cascade. Returns substrate-typed measurement of information
# loss between source's typing discipline and artifact's runtime-
# preserved structure.
#
# Returns `imperfect<npm_artifact, ref, information_loss>` — the
# loss slot carries measured loss as substrate-typed data, NOT
# Shannon, NOT estimation; the composite of @epistemologic/properties
# per [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]].
#
# The measurement IS substrate-architectural: read the source's
# typing-discipline use (row poly, ADT count, type class instances,
# HKT positions, rank-N quantifiers, functional dep triggers); read
# the artifact's runtime-preserved structure from the unlabel'd
# module's externs + the labeled metadata; compute the dimension gap.
#
# requires ps_npm_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p): bilateral
# that the measurement IS computable. Per hedge 4: FFI bounds the
# measurement to the typed sub-program; the bilateral discharges
# with a Narcissus-warned verdict for FFI-present programs.
#
# Per Alex 2026-06-23 (verbatim): "math, not vibes." This action
# operationalizes that at the Purescript-npm altitude.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
measure_ps_npm(source: purescript_source, artifact: npm_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect(npm_artifact, ref, information_loss)
requires ps_npm_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p)
{ \ }

# === purescript_well_typed bilateral ===
#
# Source-side typing-discipline bilateral. Specializes the family-
# root's grammar_coherent at source_grammar=purescript.
#
# Splinter-pole: well-typed by `purs compile`; FFI (if present)
# correctly annotated at the boundary; loss measurement complete-
# capable.
# Narcissus-pole: type errors OR FFI annotations ill-formed at the
# boundary. Compilation cannot proceed.
# Narcissus-warned (per hedge 4): FFI annotations well-formed but
# FFI code outside typing discipline; measurement bounded to typed
# sub-program; FFI gap unmeasurable by this species.
purescript_well_typed(source: purescript_source, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === npm_consumable bilateral ===
#
# Target-side packaging-well-formedness bilateral. Commitment that
# the (module, metadata) pair forms a coherent npm package.
#
# Splinter-pole: metadata.name matches npm naming rules; version
# is valid semver; entry resolves inside the module's emitted files;
# exports map (if present) resolves across all subpath conditions.
# Narcissus-pole: registry would reject OR consumer `require`/
# `import` resolution would fail.
npm_consumable(module: purescript_module, metadata: npm_metadata, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === ps_npm_loss_well_defined bilateral ===
#
# Specializes the family-root's loss_well_defined for this cascade.
# Commitment that the substrate-typed gap calculation IS computable
# for the (source, artifact) pair.
#
# Splinter-pole: externs readable from the artifact's unlabel'd
# module; composite of @epistemologic/properties dischargeable;
# measurement bounded and substrate-typed.
# Narcissus-pole: externs missing (bundler stripped them);
# substrate cannot read the typing residue; measurement undefined.
# Narcissus-warned: externs present but cover only the typed
# sub-program (FFI gap unmeasurable; per hedge 4).
ps_npm_loss_well_defined(source: purescript_source, artifact: npm_artifact, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === ps_npm_cascade_well_formed composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral. Specializes the family-root's
# cascade_well_defined for this cascade. Composes the three sub-
# predicates at this altitude.
#
# requires purescript_well_typed(source, p): source-side typing
# discipline IS coherent.
# requires npm_consumable(unlabel(artifact, p), label_of(artifact, p), p):
# target-side packaging IS well-formed; uses @labeled.unlabel +
# @labeled.label_of to extract module and metadata from the artifact.
# requires ps_npm_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p): loss
# measurement IS computable.
#
# All three must hold; substrate refuses cascade if source has type
# errors OR packaging is malformed OR measurement is undefined.
#
# Splinter-pole: all three discharge; substrate-typed loss returned.
# Narcissus-pole: at least one sub-predicate fails; cascade blocked.
# Narcissus-warned: all three discharge but at least one is warned
# (e.g., FFI present); cascade operates with bounded measurement;
# warning propagates to caller.
#
# Same composed-bilateral pattern as @cascade.cascade_well_defined
# (the family-root) and forward-promised species (gleam-js, rust-
# wasm, scala-jvm). The discipline pattern is altitude-portable.
ps_npm_cascade_well_formed(source: purescript_source, artifact: npm_artifact, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires purescript_well_typed(source, p)
requires npm_consumable(unlabel(artifact, p), label_of(artifact, p), p)
requires ps_npm_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p)
{ \ }

out @cascade/code/purescript/js
out purescript_source
out purescript_module
out npm_artifact
out npm_metadata
out compile_ps
out bundle_npm
out measure_ps_npm
out purescript_well_typed
out npm_consumable
out ps_npm_loss_well_defined
out ps_npm_cascade_well_formed
